hey guys goodness I have a fitness app  you get to workout life with me and  other amazing trainers every single day  go on down appear on the App Store or go  to fear live.com and start your journey  to become let's face it sometimes life  as a student can be hectic and when  you're living away from home you may be  restricted to very limited cooking  utensils hence you feel like you can't  be healthy although you're trying really  hard to I'm going to show you how as a  student you can still eat healthy using  very basic kitchen utensils and cooking  ingredients plus you don't need any  cooking skills because trust me I barely  knew anything when I was a student  this meal prep only required to have  ingredients to make breakfast lunch and  dinner for a total of three days the  chopped ingredients are bread tortilla  soba or rice noodles tomato paste black  beans corn carrots bell pepper chicken  leg onions eggs and cheese as students I  know that we always want to have a  variety especially when it comes to our  meals so remember these ingredients can  be easily replaced with something else  as long as you have the basis of the  recipes right I'm super excited about  breakfast because we're making pizza  bread yes I personally used to make this  when I was a student living in a school  hostel it's really simple plus the idea  of having pizza for breakfast is great  only four ingredients two slices of  homeo bread two hard-boiled eggs tomato  paste and cheese now let's start by  prepping the eggs boil them until they  are hard once the eggs are ready  thinly slice using an egg slicer then  spread about one tablespoon of tomato  paste evenly over each slice of bread  and top it up with the sliced eggs  finally sprinkle some cheese on top just  about 1 tablespoon on both if you have a  toaster oven  simply bake for 5 to 7 minutes until the  cheese is melted and the bread toasted  if not you can also place it onto a pan  and allow the bread to toast then cover  it for a couple of minutes until the  cheese melts well if you know that  you're always in a morning rush to go  for your classes  then boil lots of eggs the day before  and store them in the fridge for up to  three days all you have to do in the  morning is to assemble this dish which  takes less than 10 minutes egg is a  power food because it is a great source  of protein just consuming 2 eggs in the  morning you're already getting 12 grams  of protein you want to be having protein  in the morning because it helps to keep  you full and satisfied  this means no snacking in between plus  you get to stay focused throughout your  morning classes it's lunchtime I'm going  to keep it really simple  and here this you don't even have to  cook you can prep ahead and pack this  with you to school we're making vegan  black bean and corn wrap for this you'll  need tortillas one can of black beans  washed and drained 1/3 cup of corn  washed and drained 1 red bell pepper 1/2  an onion and tomato paste start by  dicing the onion and bell pepper then in  a bowl simply mix all the ingredients  together I'm going to season it with a  little bit of salt and pepper to  assemble grab one tortilla and spread  about one tablespoon of tomato paste  onto it then scoop about a quarter cup  of the mixed ingredients and spread it  onto one side of the tortilla now  carefully and gently roll it up and  press it down firmly  you can have about two tortilla wraps  for lunch and I like to serve mine with  more sliced up vegetables on the side  what I like to do is prep the mixed  ingredients and store it in the fridge  for up to three days and when I want to  have it all I have to do is assemble it  into a wrap that way I'm always keeping  my lunch fresh and what I like about  this recipe is that you can simply  change up the ingredients for instance  use tuna chickpeas or even chicken  breasts and the same goes to the  vegetables choose cucumber cherry  tomatoes olives or carrots as for dinner  let's make a hearty bowl of soup noodles  from my version we're going to add in a  lot of protein and also vegetables and  instead of cooking instant noodles which  are mostly deep-fried let's go for much  healthier noodles such as soba rice or  sweet potato noodles and guess what  these noodles are also gluten free for  my students I'm using one whole chicken  leg half a carrot a quarter of an onion  a quarter of a red bell pepper 2  tablespoons of corn 2 ounces of soba  noodles and an egg slice up all the  vegetables in a pot saute the onion with  about 1 TSP of sesame oil until fragrant  and slightly golden brown then pour in  about one and a half cups of water and  simply add in the ingredients chicken  leg carrots and corn I'm gonna season it  with a little bit of salt and pepper let  it simmer until the chicken leg is fully  cooked through then stir in the soba  noodles and bell pepper and allow it to  cook for another 2 to 3 minutes until  the noodles are done soup noodles always  taste so much better with an egg so I'm  going to crack an egg stir it and let it  cook for another minute I love an eggy  broth voila  dinner is ready this is a one pot dish  which has protein cups and lots of  vegetables so no fussing about in the  kitchen by trying to cook too  different dishes you can't keep changing  your protein by using fish beef pork or  even beans now if you like a stronger  broth taste you can simply add a little  bit of chicken or vegetable stock into  your cooking listen up no more excuses  for not eating healthy even if you're  living on your own try all these recipes  and let me know which is a favorite in  the comments below and do check out  other really simple a healthy student  recipes on my youtube channel so be sure  to give this video a thumbs up like this  video and share this video with your  friends and don't forget to hashtag me  and tag me in your post all the best
 

